    "done_when": "In imas_ambix/gs/description_artifact.py, four changes, nothing else. (1) DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION_ROOT and DEFAULT_MACHINE_MAP derive from imas_ambix.data.paths.JT60SA_MAP_DIR (its machine_description directory and machine_map.json), so no absolute /home path remains in the module. (2) Completeness is derived, not hard-coded: the producer authors no field_evidence and no channel_drive, so each phase artifact is created with complete=False and unresolved_gaps naming both absences in trimmed, canonically ordered text, one gap saying the channel drive map is not authored from that phase's drive topology in machine_map.json (jt60sa-pf-drive-op1 or jt60sa-pf-drive-op2) and one saying no field evidence ledger is authored. complete becomes True only when both are supplied, which this node does not do. The final resolve_machine_artifact call passes allow_incomplete=not manifest.complete. (3) Each phase's shot-range evidence comes from one module-level table keyed by phase, with a comment stating the mechanism: OP1 is observed because its description was checked against acquired OP1 pulses, and OP2 is inherited because EDDB holds no OP2 pulse, so its identity comes from the declared description alone. (4) The module docstring and the landing fragment no longer claim the whole identity is derived; they state that field evidence and channel drives are not yet authored and are named as gaps. In tests/gs/test_description_artifact.py, keep the five tests passing and add three: each artifact's member names are exactly master.h5 plus the five IDS .h5 files, with no receipt.json and no .nc file; each artifact is incomplete and names both gaps; and OP1's range evidence is observed while OP2's is inherited. Update docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-jt60sa-artifact-producer.html in place with the new semantic identities, the gaps and the evidence states, keeping the rest. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the head revision and command and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/gs/test_description_artifact.py; it exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0.",
